{"seq":1,"slug":"general-psychology","title":"心理学导论","stage":"DONE","category":"psychology","chapterCount":5,"docCount":20,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology","rating":{"composite":3.63,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":3},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.31,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":2.5}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"心理学导论-简介\">心理学导论 简介</h1><p>心理学导论是进入心理学世界的第一扇门，它系统地介绍心理学作为一门科学的基本面貌、研究方法和核心议题。本模块面向具有一定理性思维能力的技术从业者和终身学习者，帮助读者建立对人类心理与行为的科学理解框架，并将这些知识应用到日常工作与生活中。</p>\n<p>第1章<strong>心理学史与学派</strong>梳理了心理学从哲学母体中独立出来的历程，从冯特建立第一个心理学实验室，到结构主义与机能主义的早期交锋，再到行为主义革命对心理学研究范式的彻底重塑，最终抵达认知革命带来的信息加工视角。理解这些历史脉络，有助于读者把握当代心理学的多元理论根基。</p>\n<p>第2章<strong>研究方法</strong>聚焦于心理学作为实证科学的方法论基础。从科学方法的基本逻辑出发，依次介绍相关研究设计的优势与局限、质性研究方法在心理学中的独特价值，以及研究伦理对科学实践的约束。掌握这些方法论知识，能让读者批判性地评估日常接触到的心理学研究结论。</p>\n<p>第3章<strong>统计与测量</strong>为理解心理学研究提供量化工具。描述统计帮助我们概括数据特征，推断统计让我们从样本推向总体，效应量与统计效力则衡量研究发现的实际意义，信效度分析确保测量工具的科学性。这些知识构成了阅读和评价心理学文献的必备素养。</p>\n<p>第4章<strong>生物学基础概览</strong>从神经元与神经递质的微观世界出发，逐步展开到大脑结构与功能分区、内分泌系统对行为的调节，以及遗传与行为的复杂关系。这一章帮助读者理解心理现象背后的生物学机制，建立&quot;心脑一体&quot;的科学认知。</p>\n<p>第5章<strong>当代视角与趋势</strong>将视野拉回现实，介绍生物-心理-社会模型这一整合性框架，概述心理学职业发展的多元方向，探讨开放科学与可重复性危机对学科的深远影响，并专门为程序员群体解读心理学知识的实用价值。</p>\n<p>推荐学习路径为：先通读第1章建立历史感，再学习第2、3章掌握方法论工具，然后深入第4章理解生物学根基，最后通过第5章将所学知识与当代实践和个人职业发展连接起来。每一章的知识都为后续章节提供支撑，建议按序阅读。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"history-and-schools","title":"心理学史与学派","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/history-and-schools","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"history-of-psychology","title":"心理学发展简史","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/history-and-schools/history-of-psychology"},{"seq":2,"slug":"structuralism-functionalism","title":"结构主义与机能主义","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/history-and-schools/structuralism-functionalism"},{"seq":3,"slug":"behaviorism-revolution","title":"行为主义革命","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/history-and-schools/behaviorism-revolution"},{"seq":4,"slug":"cognitive-revolution","title":"认知革命","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/history-and-schools/cognitive-revolution"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"research-methods","title":"研究方法","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/research-methods","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"scientific-method","title":"科学方法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/research-methods/scientific-method"},{"seq":2,"slug":"correlational-research","title":"相关研究","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/research-methods/correlational-research"},{"seq":3,"slug":"qualitative-methods","title":"质性研究方法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/research-methods/qualitative-methods"},{"seq":4,"slug":"ethics-in-research","title":"研究伦理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/research-methods/ethics-in-research"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"statistics-and-measurement","title":"统计与测量","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/statistics-and-measurement","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"descriptive-statistics","title":"描述统计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/statistics-and-measurement/descriptive-statistics"},{"seq":2,"slug":"inferential-statistics","title":"推断统计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/statistics-and-measurement/inferential-statistics"},{"seq":3,"slug":"effect-size-power","title":"效应量与统计效力","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/statistics-and-measurement/effect-size-power"},{"seq":4,"slug":"reliability-validity","title":"信度与效度","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/statistics-and-measurement/reliability-validity"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"biological-foundations","title":"生物学基础概览","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/biological-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"neurons-neurotransmitters","title":"神经元与神经递质","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/general-psychology/